---
layout: layouts/base.njk
head: partials/home-head.njk
headerSurface: transparent
headerScrolledSurface: solid
footerSheet: true
footerFaq: true
headerHideOnScroll: true
title: dsgn.systems — your brand colour, guaranteed contrast
description: "CSS design system for any stack: pick any brand colour and every text, border and focus pair still passes WCAG 2.2 AA, light and dark. Plain HTML, a Figma library checked against the code, a skill for AI agents."
ogDescription: Pick any brand colour and every pair still passes WCAG 2.2 AA. Plain HTML for any stack, a Figma library checked against the code.
---
    <!-- Hero as a technical sheet (Swiss, data-log): cells divided by 1 px ink rules on the 12-column
         grid, holding only information. It is the first band of one page-long sheet; the sections
         below continue it with no gap, thematic groups on. The promise is the one thing no other kit
         makes: any brand colour, contrast guaranteed. The two calls to action are in the header, which comes back
         as soon as the page scrolls up; the hero keeps the install line. -->
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet hero-sheet">
          <p class="sheet-cell sheet-meta" data-span="quarter" data-tone="sunken">CSS design system for any stack</p>
          <p class="sheet-cell sheet-meta" data-span="quarter" data-tone="sunken"><span class="sheet-key">WCAG</span> 2.2 AA in any colour</p>
          <p class="sheet-cell sheet-meta" data-span="quarter" data-tone="sunken"><span class="sheet-key">Figma</span> Checked against code</p>
          <p class="sheet-cell sheet-meta" data-span="quarter" data-tone="sunken"><span class="sheet-key">Licence</span> MIT, free</p>

          <div class="sheet-cell hero-title-cell">
            <h1 class="hero-title" id="hero-title">Your brand colour. <span class="hero-highlight">Guaranteed contrast.</span></h1>
          </div>

          <div class="sheet-cell hero-lead-cell" data-span="half">
            <p class="dsgn-lead">Pick any colour and every text, border and focus ring still passes WCAG&nbsp;2.2&nbsp;AA, in light and dark. {{ components.count }} components in plain HTML for any stack, and a Figma library the build checks against the&nbsp;code.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell hero-install-cell" data-span="half">
            <div class="install">
              <code class="install-command" id="install-command">npm i dsgn.systems</code>
              <button class="dsgn-icon-button" data-variant="ghost" data-intent="neutral" type="button" data-copy="npm i dsgn.systems" aria-label="Copy install command">
                <span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Numbers: what a buyer weighs (coverage, weight, effort), each with the fact behind it. -->
    <section class="dsgn-section sheet-section" aria-label="dsgn in numbers">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet">
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-stat">
              <p class="dsgn-stat-label">Colour pairs that pass WCAG</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-value">{{ dsgn.contrast.pass }} / {{ dsgn.contrast.pairs }}</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-meta">for any brand colour, checked for every hue on every build</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-stat">
              <p class="dsgn-stat-label">Components</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-value">{{ components.count }}</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-meta">plus layout primitives, each one also in Figma</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-stat">
              <p class="dsgn-stat-label">CSS, minified and gzipped</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-value">{{ dsgn.size.css }} kB</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-meta">plus {{ dsgn.size.js }} kB of optional JavaScript</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-stat">
              <p class="dsgn-stat-label">Build steps in your project</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-value">0</p>
              <p class="dsgn-stat-meta">plain HTML in any framework, CMS or static page</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Modes: one card, one attribute at a time, laid out like The scale. The brand colour comes first:
         main.js changes the attributes in turn until a value is picked, home-brand.js recolours the card
         with the theme engine and shows its contrast check; the legend marks every current value.
         Without a brand the card is monochrome, and it takes glass here (in dsgn only chrome does). -->
    <section class="dsgn-section sheet-section" id="modes" aria-labelledby="modes-title">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet">
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-head" data-tone="sunken">
            <div class="sheet-head-text">
              <p class="sheet-meta sheet-key">Try it</p>
              <h2 class="dsgn-display" id="modes-title">Your brand, every mode, one attribute.</h2>
              <p class="dsgn-body">Pick a colour: the card is recoloured by the same theme engine that <code>npx dsgn theme</code> runs, and every colour pair is checked as you go. Then switch the modes on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> or any section; the markup stays the same.</p>
            </div>
            <a class="dsgn-button" data-variant="subtle" data-intent="neutral" href="{{ site.links.themeCustomizer }}">Theme customizer<span class="dsgn-icon" data-end aria-hidden="true">arrow_forward</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-flush preview-cell" data-span="half">
            <div class="preview">
              <div class="preview-card" id="preview" data-brand="#2f6fed" data-theme="light" data-density="m" data-radius="default" data-elevation="flat" data-lines="on" data-material="solid" inert>
                <article class="dsgn-card">
                  <div class="dsgn-cluster" data-justify="between" data-nowrap>
                    <h3 class="dsgn-card-title">Invoice 2026-114</h3>
                    <span class="dsgn-badge" data-intent="success">Paid</span>
                  </div>
                  <dl class="dsgn-dl">
                    <div><dt>Client</dt><dd>Studio Kolo s.r.o.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Total</dt><dd>CZK 24&nbsp;200</dd></div>
                  </dl>
                  <label class="dsgn-choice"><input type="checkbox" class="dsgn-switch" role="switch" checked> Overdue reminders</label>
                  <div class="dsgn-card-actions">
                    <button class="dsgn-button" data-variant="subtle" data-intent="neutral" type="button"><span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">download</span>PDF</button>
                    <button class="dsgn-button" type="button">Send reminder</button>
                  </div>
                </article>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-flush" data-span="half">
            <ol class="modes-legend" id="modes-legend">
              <li data-attr="brand">
                <span class="step-index">01</span>
                <div class="mode-text">
                  <p><strong>Brand colour</strong> <code>dsgn.theme.mjs</code></p>
                  <p>Any hue. Lightness stays fixed per step, so contrast holds.</p>
                  <div class="mode-values" role="group" aria-label="Brand colour">
                    {%- for c in [["#2f6fed", "blue"], ["#ff4400", "orange"], ["#0f8a5f", "green"], ["#7a3fd1", "violet"], ["#d6336c", "pink"], ["mono", "mono"]] %}<button type="button" data-value="{{ c[0] }}" aria-pressed="false">{% if c[0] != "mono" %}<span class="mode-swatch" style="--swatch: {{ c[0] }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}{{ c[1] }}</button>{% endfor %}
                  </div>
                  <p class="sc-contrast brand-check" id="brand-check" data-intent="success"><span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">check_circle</span><span>All {{ dsgn.contrast.pairs }} colour pairs pass WCAG, light and dark</span></p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li data-attr="theme">
                <span class="step-index">02</span>
                <div class="mode-text">
                  <p><strong>Theme</strong> <code>data-theme</code></p>
                  <p>Light or dark; every text and border pair is checked in both.</p>
                  <div class="mode-values" role="group" aria-label="Theme"><button type="button" data-value="light" aria-pressed="false">light</button><button type="button" data-value="dark" aria-pressed="false">dark</button></div>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li data-attr="density">
                <span class="step-index">03</span>
                <div class="mode-text">
                  <p><strong>Density</strong> <code>data-density</code></p>
                  <p>Padding and line height of controls, 44&nbsp;px targets on touch.</p>
                  <div class="mode-values" role="group" aria-label="Density"><button type="button" data-value="s" aria-pressed="false">s</button><button type="button" data-value="m" aria-pressed="false">m</button><button type="button" data-value="l" aria-pressed="false">l</button></div>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li data-attr="radius">
                <span class="step-index">04</span>
                <div class="mode-text">
                  <p><strong>Radius</strong> <code>data-radius</code></p>
                  <p>Corners, from square to pill.</p>
                  <div class="mode-values" role="group" aria-label="Radius"><button type="button" data-value="sharp" aria-pressed="false">sharp</button><button type="button" data-value="default" aria-pressed="false">default</button><button type="button" data-value="rounded" aria-pressed="false">rounded</button><button type="button" data-value="pill" aria-pressed="false">pill</button></div>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li data-attr="elevation">
                <span class="step-index">05</span>
                <div class="mode-text">
                  <p><strong>Elevation</strong> <code>data-elevation</code></p>
                  <p>Borders only, or soft shadows.</p>
                  <div class="mode-values" role="group" aria-label="Elevation"><button type="button" data-value="flat" aria-pressed="false">flat</button><button type="button" data-value="soft" aria-pressed="false">soft</button></div>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li data-attr="lines">
                <span class="step-index">06</span>
                <div class="mode-text">
                  <p><strong>Lines</strong> <code>data-lines</code></p>
                  <p>Outlines and separators, separators only, or none.</p>
                  <div class="mode-values" role="group" aria-label="Lines"><button type="button" data-value="on" aria-pressed="false">on</button><button type="button" data-value="minimal" aria-pressed="false">minimal</button><button type="button" data-value="none" aria-pressed="false">none</button></div>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li data-attr="material">
                <span class="step-index">07</span>
                <div class="mode-text">
                  <p><strong>Material</strong> <code>data-material</code></p>
                  <p>Solid or frosted glass on bars, toasts and backdrops; shown here on the card.</p>
                  <div class="mode-values" role="group" aria-label="Material"><button type="button" data-value="solid" aria-pressed="false">solid</button><button type="button" data-value="glass" aria-pressed="false">glass</button></div>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why: the three things other kits leave to you (a row each: title | text), then four that make daily work easy. -->
    <section class="dsgn-section sheet-section" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet">
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-head" data-tone="sunken">
            <div class="sheet-head-text">
              <p class="sheet-meta sheet-key">Why dsgn</p>
              <h2 class="dsgn-display" id="why-title">What other kits leave to you.</h2>
              <p class="dsgn-lead">Most UI kits hand you components and wish you luck with your colours, your Figma file and your agents. dsgn checks all three on every build.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell why-pillar" data-span="half">
            <span class="sheet-meta sheet-key feature-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <h3 class="dsgn-title">Contrast for any brand colour</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell why-pillar-text" data-span="half">
            <p class="dsgn-body">Other kits ship fixed palettes, and the contrast of your own colour is yours to check. dsgn builds its palettes in OKLCH with the lightness fixed per step, so any hue passes: {{ dsgn.contrast.pairs }} text, border and focus pairs are checked across every hue, light and dark, before a release.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell why-pillar" data-span="half">
            <span class="sheet-meta sheet-key feature-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <h3 class="dsgn-title">A Figma library that stays in step</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell why-pillar-text" data-span="half">
            <p class="dsgn-body">Figma kits usually drift from the code within months. dsgn&rsquo;s library has the same tokens, components, modes and version number as the package, and the build fails when the two differ. Every component carries its markup, so handoff is a copy and paste.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell why-pillar" data-span="half">
            <span class="sheet-meta sheet-key feature-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <h3 class="dsgn-title">Built for AI agents</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell why-pillar-text" data-span="half">
            <p class="dsgn-body">The package ships a <a class="dsgn-link" href="{{ site.links.skill }}">skill</a> that teaches coding agents to build with dsgn, with a definition of done for accessibility, SEO, form security and performance. <code>npx dsgn lint</code> keeps their CSS, and yours, on the tokens: no stray pixels, no stray colours.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-feature" data-layout="stack">
              <span class="sheet-meta sheet-key feature-index" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
              <div class="dsgn-feature-body">
                <h3 class="dsgn-feature-title">Plain HTML, any stack</h3>
                <p class="dsgn-feature-text">Classes and data attributes on native elements. React, a CMS template or a static page, no build step.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-feature" data-layout="stack">
              <span class="sheet-meta sheet-key feature-index" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
              <div class="dsgn-feature-body">
                <h3 class="dsgn-feature-title">Your CSS always wins</h3>
                <p class="dsgn-feature-text">Everything ships in cascade layers, so one plain rule overrides it. No <code>!important</code>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-feature" data-layout="stack">
              <span class="sheet-meta sheet-key feature-index" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
              <div class="dsgn-feature-body">
                <h3 class="dsgn-feature-title">Accessible by default</h3>
                <p class="dsgn-feature-text">WCAG 2.2 AA tested with axe, keyboard and forced colours on every build.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell" data-span="quarter">
            <div class="dsgn-feature" data-layout="stack">
              <span class="sheet-meta sheet-key feature-index" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
              <div class="dsgn-feature-body">
                <h3 class="dsgn-feature-title">Documented with examples</h3>
                <p class="dsgn-feature-text">Every component with live examples, its markup and when to use it, in the <a class="dsgn-link" href="{{ site.links.docs }}">docs</a>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Showcase: one cell per demo with its screen (site/scripts/showcase-shots.mjs), each in its own brand. -->
    <section class="dsgn-section sheet-section" id="showcase" aria-labelledby="showcase-title">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet">
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-head" data-tone="sunken">
            <div class="sheet-head-text">
              <p class="sheet-meta sheet-key">Showcase</p>
              <h2 class="dsgn-display" id="showcase-title">One system, any brand.</h2>
              <p class="dsgn-body">Two real screens built only from dsgn components, each in its own brand. Open one, give it your colour, corners and density, and copy the theme when it looks right.</p>
            </div>
            <a class="dsgn-button" data-variant="subtle" data-intent="neutral" href="{{ site.links.showcase }}">All demos<span class="dsgn-icon" data-end aria-hidden="true">arrow_forward</span></a>
          </div>
          <article class="sheet-cell sheet-card demo-card" data-span="half">
            <div class="dsgn-media dsgn-card-media"><img src="/img/showcase/billing.jpg" alt="" width="1656" height="1034" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
            <h3 class="dsgn-card-title"><a class="dsgn-card-link" href="/showcase/billing/">Billing app</a></h3>
            <p class="dsgn-card-text">An invoicing tool in blue: app shell, stats, tabs and a table of invoices with statuses.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="sheet-cell sheet-card demo-card" data-span="half">
            <div class="dsgn-media dsgn-card-media"><img src="/img/showcase/shop.jpg" alt="" width="1656" height="1034" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
            <h3 class="dsgn-card-title"><a class="dsgn-card-link" href="/showcase/shop/">Shop product page</a></h3>
            <p class="dsgn-card-text">A ceramics shop in terracotta, rounded and soft: gallery, ratings, option cards, a cart toast and reviews.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Figma: the variable collections as cells, no table to scroll sideways. -->
    <section class="dsgn-section sheet-section" id="figma" aria-labelledby="figma-title">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet">
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-head" data-tone="sunken">
            <div class="sheet-head-text">
              <p class="sheet-meta sheet-key">Figma</p>
              <h2 class="dsgn-display" id="figma-title">The same system on the canvas.</h2>
              <p class="dsgn-body">The library keeps the tokens as Figma variables, grouped in collections. Each mode of a collection is the same switch a developer sets in code, so designers try dark, dense or pill on a frame exactly as the page will do it. One version number covers the npm package and the library, and the build checks that they match.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="dsgn-cluster">
              {%- if site.links.figmaFile %}
              <a class="dsgn-button" data-variant="subtle" data-intent="neutral" href="{{ site.links.figmaFile }}">Figma library<span class="dsgn-icon" data-end aria-hidden="true">arrow_outward</span></a>
              {%- endif %}
              <a class="dsgn-button" data-variant="subtle" data-intent="neutral" href="{{ site.links.figmaPlugin }}">Figma theme plugin<span class="dsgn-icon" data-end aria-hidden="true">arrow_outward</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          {%- for c in dsgn.figma.collections %}{% if c.modes | length %}
          <div class="sheet-cell collection" data-span="quarter">
            <p class="sheet-meta"><span class="sheet-key">{{ c.name }}</span></p>
            <p class="collection-count">{{ c.variables }}<span class="dsgn-visually-hidden"> variables</span></p>
            <p class="collection-modes">{{ c.modes | join(" · ") }}</p>
          </div>
          {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
          <div class="sheet-cell collection" data-span="half">
            <p class="sheet-meta"><span class="sheet-key">One mode</span></p>
            <p class="collection-modes">{% for c in dsgn.figma.collections %}{% if not (c.modes | length) %}{{ c.name }} {{ c.variables }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell collection" data-span="half">
            <p class="sheet-meta"><span class="sheet-key">In total</span></p>
            <p class="collection-modes">{{ dsgn.figma.variables }} variables · {{ dsgn.figma.textStyles }} text styles · markup in every component</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Scale: a construction drawing of how dsgn sizes things, for the curious, before Get started.
         main.js steps through the legend until a step is picked; the drawing is a diagram at 1 % of its width = 1 px. -->
    <section class="dsgn-section sheet-section" id="scale" aria-labelledby="scale-title">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet">
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-head" data-tone="sunken">
            <div class="sheet-head-text">
              <p class="sheet-meta sheet-key">Under the hood</p>
              <h2 class="dsgn-display" id="scale-title">Controls are sized by type.</h2>
              <p class="dsgn-body">A button, field or select is its line of text plus padding from the spacing scale, on a 2&nbsp;px grid. Density sets the padding, and your visitor&rsquo;s font size sets the rest, so a page zoomed for reading never breaks its layout.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-flush" data-span="half">
            <div class="bp" id="bp" data-step="1" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="bp-ext" data-edge="top"></span>
              <span class="bp-ext" data-edge="bottom"></span>
              <span class="bp-guide" data-edge="text-top"></span>
              <span class="bp-guide" data-edge="text-bottom"></span>
              <span class="bp-box"><span class="bp-pad" data-edge="top"></span><span class="bp-pad" data-edge="bottom"></span></span>
              <span class="bp-text"><span>Aa</span></span>
              <span class="bp-dim" data-part="pad-top"><span class="bp-val"></span></span>
              <span class="bp-dim" data-part="line"><span class="bp-val"></span></span>
              <span class="bp-dim" data-part="pad-bottom"><span class="bp-val"></span></span>
              <span class="bp-dim" data-part="height"><span class="bp-val"></span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-flush" data-span="half">
            <ol class="bp-legend" id="bp-legend">
              <li><button type="button" data-step="1"><span class="step-index">01</span><span><strong>Type</strong> 14&nbsp;px text on a 20&nbsp;px line, from the type scale.</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button" data-step="2"><span class="step-index">02</span><span><strong>Padding</strong> Space from the spacing scale, above and below: 20 + 2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;8 = 36.</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button" data-step="3"><span class="step-index">03</span><span><strong>Density S</strong> Less padding for dense screens: 20 + 2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;4 = 28.</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button" data-step="4"><span class="step-index">04</span><span><strong>Density L</strong> Larger text and padding for touch: 24 + 2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10 = 44.</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button" data-step="5"><span class="step-index">05</span><span><strong>Your font size</strong> At 20&nbsp;px in the browser everything grows by a quarter and snaps back to the 2&nbsp;px grid: 26 + 2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10 = 46.</span></button></li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Get started: one row per step, what to do on the left, the line to paste on the right. -->
    <section class="dsgn-section sheet-section" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <div class="dsgn-container">
        <div class="sheet">
          <div class="sheet-cell sheet-head" data-tone="sunken">
            <div class="sheet-head-text">
              <p class="sheet-meta sheet-key">Get started</p>
              <h2 class="dsgn-display" id="start-title">Three steps to your first page.</h2>
              <p class="dsgn-body">With npm in a project that has a build: install, import, add your brand. On a page without a build, use one of the two lines below the steps instead.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ol class="sheet-list">
            <li class="sheet-row">
              <div class="sheet-cell step" data-span="half">
                <p class="step-index">01</p>
                <div class="step-text"><h3 class="dsgn-card-title">Install</h3><p class="dsgn-card-text">The CSS, the optional script, the <code>dsgn</code> command line tool and the skill for AI agents.</p></div>
              </div>
              <div class="sheet-cell step-code" data-span="half"><div class="install"><code class="install-command">npm i dsgn.systems</code><button class="dsgn-icon-button" data-variant="ghost" data-intent="neutral" type="button" data-copy="npm i dsgn.systems" aria-label="Copy install command"><span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span></button></div></div>
            </li>
            <li class="sheet-row">
              <div class="sheet-cell step" data-span="half">
                <p class="step-index">02</p>
                <div class="step-text"><h3 class="dsgn-card-title">Import the CSS</h3><p class="dsgn-card-text">In your main stylesheet. Your own rules after it always win.</p></div>
              </div>
              <div class="sheet-cell step-code" data-span="half"><div class="install"><code class="install-command">@import "dsgn.systems/css";</code><button class="dsgn-icon-button" data-variant="ghost" data-intent="neutral" type="button" data-copy="@import &quot;dsgn.systems/css&quot;;" aria-label="Copy the import"><span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span></button></div></div>
            </li>
            <li class="sheet-row">
              <div class="sheet-cell step" data-span="half">
                <p class="step-index">03</p>
                <div class="step-text"><h3 class="dsgn-card-title">Add your brand</h3><p class="dsgn-card-text">Colour, corners and density, checked for contrast before anything is written, plus a matching Figma mode. Or try it in the <a class="dsgn-link" href="{{ site.links.themeCustomizer }}">theme customizer</a>.</p></div>
              </div>
              <div class="sheet-cell step-code" data-span="half"><div class="install"><code class="install-command">npx dsgn theme --init</code><button class="dsgn-icon-button" data-variant="ghost" data-intent="neutral" type="button" data-copy="npx dsgn theme --init" aria-label="Copy theme command"><span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span></button></div></div>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="sheet-cell sheet-meta"><span class="sheet-key">No build step?</span> Instead of 01 and 02, pick one of these</p>
          <ol class="sheet-list" type="A">
            <li class="sheet-row">
              <div class="sheet-cell step" data-span="half">
                <p class="step-index">A</p>
                <div class="step-text"><h3 class="dsgn-card-title">Copy the files</h3><p class="dsgn-card-text">Puts <code>dsgn.css</code> and <code>dsgn.js</code> in <code>vendor/dsgn/</code>; link them like your own files. Everything stays on your domain. Run it again to update.</p></div>
              </div>
              <div class="sheet-cell step-code" data-span="half"><div class="install"><code class="install-command">npx dsgn copy</code><button class="dsgn-icon-button" data-variant="ghost" data-intent="neutral" type="button" data-copy="npx dsgn copy" aria-label="Copy the copy command"><span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span></button></div></div>
            </li>
            <li class="sheet-row">
              <div class="sheet-cell step" data-span="half">
                <p class="step-index">B</p>
                <div class="step-text"><h3 class="dsgn-card-title">Link the CDN</h3><p class="dsgn-card-text">Nothing to install: the files come from jsDelivr. Pin the minor version. The script is optional; add it for tabs, menus, tooltips and toasts.</p></div>
              </div>
              {%- set cdn = "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dsgn.systems@" + dsgn.minor + "/dist/dsgn.min" %}
              <div class="sheet-cell step-code" data-span="half"><div class="install"><code class="install-command">&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ cdn }}.css"&gt;<br>&lt;script src="{{ cdn }}.js" defer&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code><button class="dsgn-icon-button" data-variant="ghost" data-intent="neutral" type="button" data-copy="&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;{{ cdn }}.css&quot;&gt;&#10;&lt;script src=&quot;{{ cdn }}.js&quot; defer&gt;&lt;/script&gt;" aria-label="Copy the CDN lines"><span class="dsgn-icon" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span></button></div></div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <script type="module" src="/home-brand.js"></script>

